task: solo-part
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/solo-part
worktree: ../okay-wt-solo

why: the operator's question — how do we make a rising producer count
  cost nothing? The answer should not be "pick the right buffer": a
  channel does not know how many producers it will get. `AdaptiveFifo`
  already grows a part per producer (122/725/2375 for the ring against
  149/135/99 for the buffer at 1/4/16 producers), so the ONLY thing
  standing between us and a channel that never slows down is its 22%
  at ONE producer, where a plain ring is what the channel would rather
  be.

what: make the single-part case indistinguishable from a plain ring.
  A `solo` field holds the one part while there is one, so push, pop,
  hasRoom and popMany go straight to it — no `open` read, no
  AtomicReferenceArray read, no scan check. When a second producer
  claims a part, `solo` is cleared for good and the general path takes
  over.

predict: one producer 149 -> 128 or better (the ring is 122, and the
  remaining gap is one volatile read plus the extra virtual call).
  Four and sixteen producers unchanged (135 / 99).
  Disqualifying: one producer still above 140 means the cost is the
  megamorphic call site at the channel, not the lookup — and then the
  answer is the harder one, a channel that SWAPS a plain ring for a
  partitioned buffer when the second producer appears (filed instead).
